**How to use the baseline once it is complete:**
- A baseline test that passes on {{ target_ver }} **without being modified** is your evidence that
  behaviour was preserved. Say so explicitly in the report when it happens.
- Change a baseline test **only** where the API moved (a renamed field, a renamed relation).
  If one fails on real behaviour, you changed something: find out what before adjusting the
  test. Editing the assertion to match the new result destroys the instrument.
- Tests written *after* the upgrade only pin post-upgrade behaviour and cannot tell you
  whether you changed anything.
{% if not baseline.is_green %}
- The rows marked **RED** were already failing on {{ baseline.version }}, before you touched anything.
  Those failures pre-date the upgrade — do not attribute them to it, and do not go hunting
  for a regression you did not cause. Report them separately as pre-existing defects.
{% endif %}
{% if baseline.modules_not_covered %}
